;; Payables, charges, bank-stated balances and their correspondences, derived
;; from jun784@gmail.com. Loaded by the generic 90-docs reader in
;; manifest/edn-query.cljs (vector-of-maps -> one entity per record), so it is
;; queryable alongside the ADR / fleet / company planes.
;;
;; EVERY record carries :fin/evidence-message-id -- the Gmail message it came
;; from. A number without an evidence id in this file is a bug, not a shortcut:
;; the whole point is that someone can go back and read the mail that said it.
;;
;; :fin/confidence is stated wherever a value was INFERRED rather than read.
;; A matched pair (invoice <-> debit) inferred from amount and date is marked
;; :inferred with the exchange rate that makes it work, so a reader can reject
;; the match rather than inherit it silently.
;;
;; Scope: obligations and settlements. Routine personal retail (Kindle, Uber,
;; food delivery) is deliberately NOT itemised here -- it is summarised in the
;; :fin/kind :summary record. This is an invoice ledger, not a spending diary.
;;
;; NOT VERIFIED, stated so it is not mistaken for fact:
;;   - fin-payable-total-advisory amount comes from the attachment FILENAME
;;     (...Y38500.pdf). No Gmail attachment-download tool exists, so the PDF
;;     body was never read.
;;   - The account these PayPay notifications describe is addressed to
;;     カワサキ ジュン (an individual). The tax advisor addresses JK株式会社 and
;;     refers to 貴社PayPay銀行口座. Whether these are ONE account or TWO is
;;     unresolved -- see fin-open-question-account-identity. Do not wire a
;;     jk-corp funding account to these balances until that is settled.

